rint tickets regardless. That could be a regression: subtasks sort row controls built but wired to wrong setting.\n\nHmm wait: maybe tapping the direction control of the Subtasks row actually toggles the Sorting direction? Let's check: After pressing [6] in the sheet, Sorting row still \"Ascending\" and Subtasks row changed to \"Ascending\"/\"Descending\". So no.\n\nLet me test parent Sorting descending: if subtask order flips too, then subtask rows use parent sort. Steps: open sort sheet, tap Sorting direction to Descending, close, observe. Expected: parent tasks reverse (Read docs, Pay rent, Pack, Buy) and subtasks? Under correct behavior subtask sort still By title Ascending → Charge then Print. If subtasks flip to Print then Charge, it's a bug (subtask sort ignored). But regardless, subtasks setting appears no effect.\n\nLet me try."}
