{"type": "thinking", "text": "List snippets are NOT linkified (plain gray text). Is that expected? The changed feature says \"web links are now detected when the note is displayed.\" Perhaps in the task list, notes are displayed as snippet; maybe links should be detected there too? Hmm, but in the list, the row is not a text view for interaction; likely detection only in edit screen. \"when the note is displayed\" — ambiguous.\n\nAlso interesting: in the list screenshot, snippets are clamped with ellipsis (single line? \"Link test\" shows 2 lines then \"...\"). Fine.\n\nAlso note the list screenshot with Show full date ON shows \"Nov 19\" etc.\n\nThe key issue I see: link detection works in the edit screen (when Show links on). So probably no bug there for basic case. But maybe the seeded bug is that links in the *snippet* are not detected even though the setting is on. The changelog says \"web links are now detected when the note is displayed\" — the note is displayed in the task list (snippet) and edit screen. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the setting \"Show links\" is what's seeded: it's OFF by default, so links aren't detected. But changed build should detect web links; maybe the intended default is ON? The precondition link is in Read docs notes, and the QA area is \"task notes and links\". The test instruction says \"web links are now detected when the note is displayed.\" If Show links defaults off, then in a fresh install the feature is invisible — but that's a setting, not a bug per se.\n\nHmm, let me think about what a seeded bug in link detection would look like. Likely a specific link form fails: e.g., links in notes are detected in edit screen but not when note is displayed elsewhere (list snippet); or detection includes trailing punctuation; or detection only detects one link per note (our test had multiple links, all detected? Let's verify by screenshot: In the editor, \"https://example.com/a\" underlined; \"www.example.com\" underlined; \"http://test.org?q=1\"