d-only). Could use Python if available in the sandbox? The instructions say we can't read app code/files/db, but we can process screenshots. However no shell tool is provided! Only device tools plus file_report. No bash. So no.\n\nI can rely on the visual. The preview 1080x2400 is fairly clear. Let me re-open Link test and screenshot closer (maybe rotate or scroll to center link line). Actually I could zoom by rotating? no. The editor shows the text at font ~. Let me re-open Link test task and take screenshot, then look carefully.\n\nBut is this worth reporting? The main obvious functional link behavior: links styled but not clickable because tapping enters edit mode. Could be the seeded bug: \"web links are now detected when the note is displayed\" but tap should open; instead tap just focuses. Hmm.\n\nLet me test again carefully: open Link test task, ensure the note field is NOT focused, then tap right on a link once. Earlier I did on Read docs and got keyboard. On Link test, tap gave selection menu (because maybe the tap lasted long?). Then after dismissing, keyboard appeared. So tap on link focuses field.\n\nBut maybe the correct interaction: tap the note once to focus (shows link), then tap the link again to open? When focused, the keyboard was open and link still underlined? Let me test: In edit screen with note focused, tap the link. If it opens browser, then links are clickable when focused. Let's test on Read docs or Link test. Open Link test."}
