{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now clearly: the third line \"example.com\" IS underlined and purple — actually looking at this screenshot: line 3 \"example.com\" appears purple and underlined! Hmm, wait the whole \"*example.com*\" appears purple with underline. Yes! The last line \"example.com\" is linkified! Interesting — perhaps the link span matched \"https://example.com\" ignoring \"(\" and the comma, and the bare \"example.com\" at end? Hmm no.\n\nLet me parse: The note text is:\n\"https://example.com/a, www.example.com, http://test.org?q=1, (https://example.com/b), example.com\"\n\nLine 1: \"https://example.com/a, www.example.com,\"\nLine 2: \"http://test.org?q=1, (https://example.com/b),\"\nLine 3: \"example.com\"\n\nIn the screenshot, line 3 \"example.com\" is purple underlined. So bare domain IS detected. That's an improvement (Linkify might detect domains without scheme if configured). Fine, not a bug.\n\nThe parentheses: line 2 shows \"(https://example.com/b)\" — the opening \"(\" appears black (not purple)? Looking at the image: \"http://test.org?q=1, (https://example.com/b),\" — the \"(\" is black, then \"https://example.com/b\" purple underlined, then \"),\" maybe black. Good — Linkify handles parentheses correctly.\n\nTrailing commas: line 1 \"https://example.com/a,\" — comma black. \"www.example.com,\" — comma after? At the right edge, the comma seems black. Good.\n\nSo link detection works well. The link handling area seems fine. Maybe test with Show links OFF to see it doesn't style (expected) and with rotation.\n\nWait, but there's the task list snippet: not linkified. Is that intended? The list snippet is displayed with note preview; maybe detection should apply there too. In the list screenshot, \"See https://example.com/guide\" appeared plain gray, not underlined/colored. In the app, list rows are clickable as a whole, so making links in snippets clickable is odd. The changed feature likely pertains to the edit screen note display only. Fine.\n\nLet me test link detection at the task list after the app restart? Not needed.\n\nNow due date grouping. Let me create a task due today to test heading. Actually, I could use the existing Link test task and set its due date to today, then examine grouping. Then delete it anyway. That avoids extra tasks. Let me set Link test due today.\n\nCurrent screen: Link test editor. Tap due date row [??]. Current observe: due date row isn't in list? The screen scrolled; due_date_row above viewport. Let me scroll up (swipe down) to top."}
